menu "OTA Signature Gate fixture (task 4.4 self-test only)"

    choice GATE_SELF_TEST_MODE
        prompt "Case scope this build runs"
        default GATE_SELF_TEST_MODE_FULL
        help
            The real gate (default) always runs all three cases in order:
            reject (tampered), reject (foreign key), accept (valid) - D5.

            Task 4.4 needs a build with signature verification compiled out
            in which the tampered and foreign-key cases are both *accepted*
            (design.md D3's discriminating self-test). sdf_ota_verify_and_
            commit() reboots unconditionally on a successful commit
            (sdf_ota.c:472) and does not return, so two cases that both
            accept cannot both run to completion in the same boot. These
            two extra choices let the self-test exercise the tampered and
            foreign-key cases as two separate emulator runs of the same
            no-verify build instead. Never used by the real gate; only
            selected by scripts/run_ota_signature_gate.sh --no-verify via
            sdkconfig.no_verify_tampered.defaults / sdkconfig.no_verify_
            foreign_key.defaults.

        config GATE_SELF_TEST_MODE_FULL
            bool "Run all three cases (real gate)"

        config GATE_SELF_TEST_MODE_TAMPERED_ONLY
            bool "Run only the tampered case, expecting ACCEPT (task 4.4)"

        config GATE_SELF_TEST_MODE_FOREIGN_KEY_ONLY
            bool "Run only the foreign-key case, expecting ACCEPT (task 4.4)"
    endchoice

endmenu
